PORT=3013
JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-in-production
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://quant:quant@localhost:5432/quantdb

# QuantCooks backend (Fastify, port 3013) — the Next API proxy target.
QUANTEDITS_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3013

# Object storage for assets (P0-3, via @quant/storage — S3/R2/MinIO).
# Set a QuantCooks bucket explicitly; without one the resolver falls back to
# the shared quantmail-attachments default. Without any storage env the
# upload endpoints fail closed with 503 STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED.
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://s3.example.com   (or R2_ENDPOINT / CLOUDFLARE_R2_ENDPOINT)
# S3_ACCESS_KEY=                       (or R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID)
# S3_SECRET_KEY=                       (or R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY)
# S3_BUCKET=quantcooks-assets          (or R2_BUCKET / ATTACHMENTS_BUCKET)
# ASSET_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=536870912     # optional, default 512 MiB

# Export processor (P0-4): the in-process worker that drives export jobs
# QUEUED → PROCESSING → COMPLETED/FAILED. It starts only when object storage
# above is configured; without storage it stays off and jobs honestly remain
# QUEUED. FFMPEG_PATH is set by Dockerfile.backend; local dev needs ffmpeg on
# PATH (a missing binary surfaces as FAILED jobs with the ffmpeg error).
# EXPORT_PROCESSOR_DISABLED=1          # kill switch: never start the worker
# EXPORT_WORK_DIR=/tmp/quantcooks-exports  # optional temp render dir

# Craft companion renderer (C-2, EffectCraft — dual-licensed MIT OR
# Apache-2.0; the binary is a black-box companion, never vendored or
# rebranded). EFFECTCRAFT_BIN is the ONLY way the backend locates it: an
# absolute path to the pinned v0.18.0 CLI. Install = download the release
# tarball effectcraft-0.18.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz, verify its sha256 against
# the release SHA256SUMS.txt (94d1d85691d54ba57fa86e04872fbcc426c33d1bd364f1fc976b1f607344880b),
# extract ONLY bin/effectcraft-cli (keep the tarball's LICENSE/NOTICE files
# alongside it), and point this variable at the extracted file. Unset or not
# executable → POST /craft/* answers 503 CRAFT_NOT_CONFIGURED and no renders
# can be created. The render worker also needs object storage above: a
# render claimed without storage fails honestly with STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED.
# EFFECTCRAFT_BIN=/opt/effectcraft/bin/effectcraft-cli
# CRAFT_RENDER_PROCESSOR_DISABLED=1    # kill switch: never start the worker
# EFFECTCRAFT_RENDER_TIMEOUT_MS=900000 # optional per-render timeout (default 15 min)
# CRAFT_RENDER_WORK_DIR=/tmp/quantcooks-craft  # optional temp render dir

# PhotoCraft companion (QuantCooks C-3B) — PHOTOCRAFT_BIN
#
# Photo edits (quantcooks.edit_photo / POST /photo/edits) run through the
# pinned PhotoCraft CLI (storytold suite, dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0;
# the binary is invoked as a black box — no upstream code is vendored).
# Install (pinned v0.17.0, https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/releases):
#   1. Download photocraft-0.17.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz (123,212,747 bytes) and
#      SHA256SUMS.txt from the v0.17.0 release; verify:
#        sha256(photocraft-0.17.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz) =
#        5259f9c428c8ee3478c35500ece98713561cafc050e4c9eb354a5050f36eb2b8
#      against the release's own SHA256SUMS.txt.
#   2. Extract ONLY the CLI binary from the tarball and keep the upstream
#      LICENSE-MIT / LICENSE-APACHE / NOTICE alongside it:
#        tar xzf photocraft-0.17.0-linux-x86_64.tar.gz \
#          photocraft-0.17.0-linux-x86_64/bin/photocraft-cli \
#          photocraft-0.17.0-linux-x86_64/share/doc/photocraft
#   3. Point PHOTOCRAFT_BIN at the extracted bin/photocraft-cli.
# Unset (or not executable) -> photo edits fail closed: POST /photo/edits
# answers 503 PHOTO_NOT_CONFIGURED and the edit processor does not start.
# Job claims while object storage is unconfigured fail honestly with
# STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED. Photo edits record creditCost 0 with
# metering 'not_wired' until CP-2 wires the credit ledger.
# PHOTOCRAFT_BIN=/opt/photocraft/bin/photocraft-cli
# PHOTO_EDIT_PROCESSOR_DISABLED=1     # stop the in-process photo edit processor
# PHOTOCRAFT_EDIT_TIMEOUT_MS=600000   # per-edit companion timeout (default 10 min)
# PHOTO_EDIT_WORK_DIR=/tmp/quantcooks-photo  # per-job scratch workspace parent

# FigCraft companion (QuantCooks C-7 step 4) — FIGCRAFT_BIN
#
# Design jobs (quantcooks.create_design / quantcooks.export_design) run
# through the pinned FigCraft CLI (storytold suite, dual-licensed MIT OR
# Apache-2.0; the binary is invoked as a black box — no upstream code is
# vendored). Install (pinned v0.12.1, https://github.com/storytold/figcraft/releases):
#   1. Download figcraft-0.12.1-linux-x86_64.tar.gz (94,094,269 bytes) and
#      SHA256SUMS.txt from the v0.12.1 release; verify:
#        sha256(figcraft-0.12.1-linux-x86_64.tar.gz) =
#        00a29f4cc382807d840f5d3e9b59f4c8829356789afbb956a0964918295e49dd
#      against the release's own SHA256SUMS.txt.
#   2. Extract ONLY the CLI binary from the tarball and keep the upstream
#      LICENSE-MIT / LICENSE-APACHE / NOTICE alongside it:
#        tar xzf figcraft-0.12.1-linux-x86_64.tar.gz \
#          figcraft-0.12.1-linux-x86_64/bin/figcraft-cli \
#          figcraft-0.12.1-linux-x86_64/share/doc/figcraft
#   3. Point FIGCRAFT_BIN at the extracted bin/figcraft-cli.
# Unset (or not executable) -> design jobs fail closed: the design tools
# answer 503 FIGCRAFT_NOT_CONFIGURED and the design processor does not
# start. Job claims while object storage is unconfigured fail honestly
# with STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED. Design jobs record creditCost 0 with
# metering 'not_wired' until CP-2 wires the credit ledger.
# FIGCRAFT_BIN=/opt/figcraft/bin/figcraft-cli
# DESIGN_PROCESSOR_DISABLED=1         # stop the in-process design processor
# FIGCRAFT_DESIGN_TIMEOUT_MS=600000   # per-job companion timeout (default 10 min)
# DESIGN_WORK_DIR=/tmp/quantcooks-design  # per-job scratch workspace parent

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CP-1 control plane (QuantAI tool registry: backend/tools/*)
#
# The registry itself needs no configuration: 54 manifest tools + the 2
# ratified Craft twins register at boot, Tier A live where a real surface
# exists, Tier B fail-closed with named errors. Credits are NOT wired in
# CP-1 (CP-2): tools with no rate row record creditCost 0 with metering
# 'not_wired', and the credits tools refuse CREDITS_NOT_CONFIGURED.
#
# MCP gateway (spec §9.5): the wiring ships behind this flag, default OFF.
# Turning it on mounts the quant-tools gateway at /mcp — but CP-1 issues
# NO tokens and delegated invokes still refuse DELEGATION_NOT_CONFIGURED;
# the surface opens for real only after CP-3 (delegation verification)
# and CP-4 (SSO token grant). Auth is the ecosystem SSO sign-in — there
# is deliberately NO QuantCooks API key, nothing to paste or rotate.
# QUANTCOOKS_MCP_ENABLED=1
# QUANTCOOKS_PUBLIC_MCP_URL=http://localhost:3013/mcp
#
# Backend runtime vars the code already reads (documented here so staging
# sets them deliberately; all were previously undocumented):
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# JWT_ISSUER=quantedits
# JWT_AUDIENCE=quant-ecosystem
# AUTO_EDIT_OUTPUT_DIR=/var/lib/quantcooks/auto-edit
# AUTO_EDIT_OUTPUT_BASE_URL=https://cdn.example.com/auto-edit
